<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Status-bar (small) icon for the reminder notifications.

  Android renders a notification's small icon from its ALPHA CHANNEL ONLY and
  tints it with the notification colour, so this must be a white-on-transparent
  silhouette. Without this file the Capacitor plugin falls back to
  `android.R.drawable.ic_dialog_info` (LocalNotificationManager.getDefaultSmallIcon),
  which is a fully-opaque multi-colour system asset. Flattened to alpha it is a
  featureless white blob, which is why the reminder never looked like ours.

  THE GLYPH IS THE V-AND-SLOT, and it is the SAME geometry as the web badge in
  `icons/badge-96.png`: APPLY-notifications.md §1.1 specifies exactly these three
  subpaths. One glyph on both platforms, so a reminder looks the same on the
  phone as it does in a desktop browser.

  This file has now been three different marks. It was the five bars, then the
  CUT tile (a rounded square with a slot cut out of it) at v216, and that one
  was already stale: the wordmark became the AJ lockup at v227 and this did not
  follow, because it CANNOT follow. It is a native resource — it changes only
  when someone edits this file and rebuilds.

  ALPHA-ONLY MEANS THE SLOT MUST BE A HOLE, not a painted bar — anything drawn
  gets tinted, so a "black" slot comes out the same colour as the ink and the
  cut disappears. Here that is free rather than fiddly: the gap between the
  upper arms (ending y 10.6) and the lower chevron (starting y 13.4) is empty
  canvas, not a shape, so there is nothing to tint and no evenOdd needed.

  INK BOX: x 2.6..21.4, y 3.4..20.6 — inside the 2..22 safe area, which leaves
  the ~1dp margin a status bar wants at its ~18px render size.

  ⚠️ BAKED INTO THE APK. Editing this changes nothing for anyone until a new APK
  is built AND installed; `git push` cannot deliver a native resource. Verify a
  build by DECOMPILING, never by checking that a file with this name exists —
  that check is what missed the launcher-icon bug for three releases. Run
  `aapt2 dump xmltree` against the built APK, passing this path with its file
  flag, and read the actual pathData.

  (The flag is described rather than written out because it starts with two
  hyphens, and two hyphens are illegal inside an XML comment. Writing it here
  literally is what failed this very build the first time — the same trap that
  briefly broke icon.svg with `-` `-bg` in its comment.)
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <!-- left arm of the V -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M2.6,3.4H7.2L10.1,10.6H5.5Z" />
    <!-- right arm -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M16.8,3.4H21.4L18.5,10.6H13.9Z" />
    <!-- lower chevron, below the slot -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M6.7,13.4H11.3L12,15.2L12.7,13.4H17.3L14.4,20.6H9.6Z" />
</vector>
